        "body": "Closes #335\n\n## What changed\n\n- add Deepgram pre-recorded transcription via the `/v1/listen` endpoint\n- keep existing provider behavior by appending Deepgram after AssemblyAI, Gemini, OpenAI, and FAL\n- default to `nova-3`, with `SUMMARIZE_DEEPGRAM_TRANSCRIPTION_MODEL` override support\n- preserve timestamped utterances across local media, podcast, YouTube, and link-preview paths\n- expose redacted Deepgram configuration in `summarize status`\n- update README, install/media/provider-flow/YouTube/transcriber docs, and changelog\n\n## User impact\n\nUsers can set `DEEPGRAM_API_KEY` in the shell or config `env` map and use Deepgram as an automatic transcription fallback without changing existing provider priority.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`\n- `pnpm -s build`\n- `pnpm -s check` — 573 test files; 2,915 passed, 29 skipped; coverage thresholds met\n- `pnpm -s docs:build`\n- focused provider/media/status tests — 53 passed\n- source-blind built-CLI validation for status, config override, key redaction, and provider absence\n- real built-CLI MP3 request reached Deepgram and returned the expected `401 INVALID_AUTH` for a deliberately invalid credential\n- autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n\nAuthenticated-success E2E remains the final pre-merge gate; no approved Deepgram credential is currently available in the environment, Molty vault, or repository Actions secrets.",
